-- A fixity-conflicted operator chain where, unlike fixity-conflict.l4, ONE
-- overload remains viable for the flat application: the 4-parameter VOP can
-- absorb the whole un-reassociated shape `VOP 1 2 VOP 3` (the inner marker
-- resolves as its FUNCTION-typed argument), so overload resolution sees
-- exactly one locally-succeeding candidate.
--
-- This pins the forkWithLazyFallback seam: the FixityConflict emitted in the
-- App preamble makes every branch a failure upstream, so the one-success
-- skip of the ambiguity fallback must NOT fire — the expected output is the
-- FixityConflict AND the two AmbiguousTermErrors, exactly as before the
-- lazy-fallback optimisation. If the ambiguity errors disappear from this
-- golden, the preamble-diagnostic flag has come unthreaded.

@infixl 6
GIVEN p IS A NUMBER
      q IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
p VOP q MEANS p PLUS q

@infixr 7
GIVEN p IS A STRING
      q IS A STRING
GIVETH A STRING
p VOP q MEANS p

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER
      b IS A NUMBER
      g IS A FUNCTION FROM A NUMBER AND A NUMBER TO A NUMBER
      c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
VOP MEANS g a (g b c)

chain MEANS 1 VOP 2 VOP 3
